WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.720
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am&nbsp;
going to explain the drama romance film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:11.600
called “The Terminal.” Spoilers&nbsp;
ahead! Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.960
The movie begins with a man named Victor&nbsp;
Navorski arriving at New York’s John F Kennedy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:27.040
International Airport. Victor is from a country&nbsp;
in eastern europe called Krakozhia. He is in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:33.120
US to fulfill his lifelong dream of visiting the&nbsp;
big apple. However, the man can’t speak a word&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:38.960
of English. At the airport, Victor discovers that&nbsp;
his passport is no longer valid and as a result he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:44.160
is pulled to the side by the airport security.&nbsp;
Victor is also penniless because his country’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:50.640
currency is no longer a legal tender in the US.&nbsp;
U.S. Customs and Border Protection Officer Judge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:56.000
Thurman seizes his return ticket, passport&nbsp;
and takes him to Frank Dixon, the Acting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.880
Field Commissioner of the airport. Dixon&nbsp;
attempts to tell Victor that the US government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:06.000
doesn’t recognize Krakozhia's new government&nbsp;
after a military coup plunged the country into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:12.000
a civil war while Victor was on air. Viktor is&nbsp;
not permitted to either enter the US or return&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.440
home as his passport is no longer considered&nbsp;
valid. However, Dixon feels sorry for him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:22.160
and allows him to stay in the international&nbsp;
transit lounge until the issue is resolved. 
&nbsp;

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:27.440
Dixon hands Victor some food coupons, a calling&nbsp;
card and a pager before sending him off to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:32.000
lounge. Bad at communicating in English,&nbsp;
Victor fails to gain entry into the lounge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:37.120
and gets stuck at the terminal. There, Victor,&nbsp;
who didn’t understand what Dixon was telling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:41.760
him about the military coup, finally learns&nbsp;
about the crisis at home through the images&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:46.960
and videos on the television. Seeing his&nbsp;
home in crisis, Victor breaks into tears.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:52.400
He pleads with other passengers to help him call&nbsp;
back home but everyone ignores him. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:58.160
Victor’s bad luck doesn’t end there and he somehow&nbsp;
manages to lose his meal vouchers. Dejected,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:02.960
Viktor settles in an old and run-down baggage&nbsp;
section of the airport with only his luggage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:12.320
and a Planters peanut can. Victor, who seems to&nbsp;
have an unusual love for the peanut can, uses his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:17.760
DIY skills to make himself more comfortable.
Meanwhile, Dixon’s boss Richard announces his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:22.480
retirement and informs him that he is slated&nbsp;
to take Richard’s place as the Active Field&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:27.760
commissioner if he gets the approval from&nbsp;
Washington. Dixon is elated by the news&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:32.640
and Richard advises him to not mess up the&nbsp;
inspection process. Dixon is confident about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:39.120
his promotion but he suddenly remembers a problem&nbsp;
that could derail his promotion, Victor. 
&nbsp;

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:45.040
The next day, Victor spends his entire morning&nbsp;
standing in the visa line to get a visa but to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:51.440
no avail. The visa officer Dolores Torres tells&nbsp;
him that he can’t get a visa without a passport.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:55.600
Dixon keeps an eye on him, hoping to catch&nbsp;
him breaking a law so he could have Victor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.600 --> 00:03:01.360
arrested and get rid of him. However, Victor stays&nbsp;
within the confines of the airport and the law,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:05.040
making Dixon regret helping him. 
Determined to get Viktor out of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:10.000
airport and make him someone else's problem,&nbsp;
Dixon schemes to get Viktor to leave the airport&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:16.080
by ordering guards away from a pair of exit doors&nbsp;
for five minutes. Victor takes the bait and almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:22.560
leaves the airport but he notices a CCTV camera&nbsp;
mirroring his every move and he grows suspicious.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:27.200
He eventually figures out Dixon’s ploy to get&nbsp;
him arrested for illegally entering the US&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:32.240
so he decides to stay in the terminal. 
When he isn’t bothering Visa officer Dolores,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:36.720
Victor spends his time learning about New&nbsp;
York and American culture. He slowly becomes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:41.760
good at communicating in English and starts using&nbsp;
rewards for returning stray shopping carts to pay&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:47.280
for his food. He also helps a flight attendant&nbsp;
named Amelia Warren catch her flight on time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:51.840
He develops a crush on her but only to see&nbsp;
her kissing another man some moments later.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.960 --> 00:04:00.320
Dolores also starts developing empathy for him&nbsp;
after having encountered Victor so many times.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:05.440
Dixon learns about Victor’s tactic to buy food and&nbsp;
deploys a man to stop him from using the reward&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:11.120
system. Seeing Victor eating biscuits as lunch,&nbsp;
airport food worker Enrique Cruz approaches him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:15.840
Cruz offers to provide Victor with food in&nbsp;
exchange for Victor’s help in getting Torres&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:21.040
to go on a date with him. Victor accepts the&nbsp;
offer and spends the next few days helping Cruz&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:27.120
understand Dolores’s likes and dislikes. Victor&nbsp;
learns about Dolores’s ex who cheated on her and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:37.760
warns Cruz against breaking her heart again. 
One day, Victor’s pager beeps and he rushes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:42.320
meet Dixon. The latter tells him that he has&nbsp;
found a way to get Victor out of the airport.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:47.440
He tells him about a provision in the US law&nbsp;
which allows an illegal alien who has a credible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:53.040
fear of returning to their home country to file&nbsp;
for asylum. After explaining everything to him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:58.320
Dixon asks the man on record if he has at this&nbsp;
time any fear of returning to his country.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:03.840
However, Victor answers in a no. He seemingly&nbsp;
didn’t understand what Victor explained to him and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:09.200
says that he can never be afraid of his home. 
Later, Victor again encounters Amelia talking on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:13.920
the phone with her boyfriend. She is having&nbsp;
an argument with him as he stood her up.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:18.960
Seeing her cry, Victor goes to comfort her. The&nbsp;
two talk for a while and Amelia asks if he’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:23.680
like to join her for dinner. But since Victor&nbsp;
can't leave the airport, he reluctantly refuses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:28.800
the offer. With his broken English, he tries&nbsp;
to make Amelia understand about his situation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:33.920
but she simply thinks that he’s not interested&nbsp;
in her. An embarrassed Amelia then leaves him.
&nbsp;

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:37.120
Next, we see Victor visiting&nbsp;
different shops at the airport,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:42.240
asking people for jobs. But since he lives at the&nbsp;
place and has no contact information and address,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:47.840
no one takes him seriously. One night, a bored&nbsp;
Victor starts working on an unfinished wall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:52.800
and completes it overnight. The constructor&nbsp;
contractor is stunned by his skills and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:57.520
immediately hires him. Victor finally&nbsp;
has a job which pays $19 an hour! 
&nbsp;

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:05.840
One day, the inspection team visits the airport&nbsp;
to check the day to day operations. As usual,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:11.520
Dixon tries his best to impress everyone as he is&nbsp;
desperate for the promotion. Suddenly, a foreign&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:16.160
man is seen causing a problem at the customs&nbsp;
office. He has some medicines with him, which he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:21.120
doesn't have the documents for. Dixon finds out&nbsp;
that the man is from a country near Krakozhia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:26.240
so he calls Victor to act as a translator. In&nbsp;
exchange for this, Dixon promises to help him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:31.280
get out of the airport. Victor then talks to the&nbsp;
distressed man and translates that the medicines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:36.160
are for his father. Dixon, however, says that&nbsp;
the man will have to provide legal documents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:41.280
if he wants to take the medicines out. Hearing&nbsp;
this, the personnel detain the man and confiscate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:46.480
his medicines. Victor suddenly feels sympathetic&nbsp;
towards him and lies that the medicines are for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:51.440
his goat and not his father. He then says&nbsp;
that he made a mistake while translating.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:56.640
Dixon immediately realizes Victor’s intentions.&nbsp;
He knows that he’s been reading forms about the US&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:00.960
rules, one of them which state that documents&nbsp;
for animal medications aren't required. 
&nbsp;

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:06.400
Despite Dixon threatening Victor that he wont help&nbsp;
him if he’s lying, Victor stands by his statement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:11.680
that he made a mistake in the translation. The&nbsp;
stressed man also plays along to this claim.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:16.960
Finally, after having no evidence, the officials&nbsp;
reluctantly release the man. A furious Dixon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:22.000
then grabs Victor by the neck. Meanwhile,&nbsp;
Dixon’s boss witnesses everything, leaving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:28.160
his chances of getting promoted to be very slim.
The next day, local sweeper Gupta tells everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:33.120
about how Victor helped the stressed man. As his&nbsp;
act of generosity is spread across the airport,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:38.080
he is respected and loved by everyone.&nbsp;
Later, Victor goes to Dixon’s office&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:43.600
and apologizes to him for making him look&nbsp;
bad, but Dixon is unmoved. An angry Dixon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:48.000
then says that as long as he is incharge&nbsp;
of the airport, Victor will never leave.
&nbsp;

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:53.440
Next we see Victor, with the help of his&nbsp;
friends, finally ask Amelia out for dinner.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:58.720
Amelia gladly accepts and the two head for dinner&nbsp;
at a spot inside the airport. Victor’s friends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:03.520
have redesigned the place to look like an actual&nbsp;
restaurant. At the dinner, while the two of them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:08.480
are conversing, Amelia describes how she is fed&nbsp;
up with her life. She complains about how her life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:13.360
is just about going in and out of the airport&nbsp;
and that she wants to live freely. Victor says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:18.800
that his life has been stuck in a similar way too.&nbsp;
However, he doesn’t disclose about his situation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:24.960
After a wonderful date, Amelia finally leaves&nbsp;
and the duo plan to meet again in 13 days.
&nbsp;

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:31.120
Meanwhile Victor successfully helps Enrique. He&nbsp;
and Torres become very close and eventually get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:36.560
married. Victor also starts working on something,&nbsp;
which he plans to show Amelia as a surprise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:41.920
After 13 days, Amelia finally arrives at the&nbsp;
airport but when she is about to meet Victor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:47.120
she gets called by Dixon. As he has seen her&nbsp;
being close with Victor, Dixon asks her to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:52.000
get more information about him. He also wants&nbsp;
Amelia to find out what Victor always carries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:58.160
in his can. Finally, he reveals that Victor has&nbsp;
been staying at the airport for 9 months. Shocked,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:06.800
Amelia feels that she has been lied to.
At night, an emotional Amelia meets Victor and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:12.000
discloses that she was about to break up with her&nbsp;
boyfriend as she was starting to like him. As she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:17.040
tries to go away, Victor stops her saying that&nbsp;
he wants to show her something. He then takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:22.000
her to the place where he was building something&nbsp;
and uncovers a beautiful fountain, which he made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:27.920
from broken plates. He knew that Amelia is fond&nbsp;
of Napoleon so he built a fountain exactly like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:34.080
the one Napoleon built for his wife Josephine. 
To further show his love, he opens his mystery can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:39.360
and takes out an old picture of a jazz group. He&nbsp;
says that his father is a big fan of the group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:44.560
and that he had sent each of them letters.&nbsp;
After waiting for 40 long years, he managed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:50.640
to collect signatures of every member except one.&nbsp;
As Amelia gets emotional, Victor says that the one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:55.840
member who didn't send back the autograph is Benny&nbsp;
Goldson, but his father died before he could add&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.840 --> 00:10:01.280
the final piece to his collection. However, before&nbsp;
his death, Victor made a promise that he would get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:06.720
the signature and complete the collection. Hence,&nbsp;
he travelled to America to fulfill his promise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:11.920
Victor continues that in order to meet Benny,&nbsp;
he will wait as long as he has to. He will also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:18.560
wait for Amelia since he loves her. Moved by his&nbsp;
selflessness, Amelia gets up and kisses him.
&nbsp;

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:23.520
One morning, Victor’s friends arrive and&nbsp;
notify him that the war is over in his country.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:29.120
A delighted Victor then starts celebrating with&nbsp;
the people at the airport. Amelia also arrives and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:34.560
Victor tells her the good news. She gets emotional&nbsp;
but at the same time is very happy for him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:38.800
Amelia then hands him over a legal document,&nbsp;
with the help of which he can get out of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:44.560
airport for one day. He can now visit New York&nbsp;
and get the signature of Benny Goldson. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:49.040
Victor’s happiness turns into disappointment&nbsp;
when he finds out that the paper was managed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:54.640
Amelia’s boyfriend, who is a powerful government&nbsp;
official. She eventually decided to stay with him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:59.680
but before leaving, she wanted to help Victor.
Victor then heads to Torres and hands her the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:04.800
travel pass. Seeing the pass, she at first gets&nbsp;
happy for him, but eventually realizes that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:09.920
document has to be signed by none other than&nbsp;
Dixon. Victor then reaches Dixon, who instead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:15.680
of signing his paper, hands him his passport and&nbsp;
tells him to leave America. Victor replies that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:21.120
will only leave once he can visit New York. Dixon&nbsp;
opposes this and blackmails him by saying that if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:25.840
he doesn’t leave, he will deport his illegal&nbsp;
friends back to their respective countries.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:30.960
Without hesitating for a second, Victor agrees&nbsp;
to leave America for the sake of his friends.
&nbsp;

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:34.960
As he is leaving the airport, his friends&nbsp;
try to stop him but he ignores them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:39.600
He then meets a furious Gupta who calls him&nbsp;
a coward for not rebelling against Dixon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:44.640
Despite this, he continues his way out without&nbsp;
telling Gupta the reason for his departure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:49.280
Then, an officer finally reveals why Victor&nbsp;
is leaving without visiting New York. 
&nbsp;

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:54.400
At the office, Dixon seems relaxed as he has&nbsp;
finally got rid of Victor once and for all.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:58.880
But his happiness is short lived as Gupta&nbsp;
is seen trying to stop the plane in which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:02.560
Victor is heading back home. He isn’t&nbsp;
scared of getting deported back to India&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.560 --> 00:12:07.360
as he wants Victor to fulfill his father’s&nbsp;
dream. Meanwhile, the flight to Krakozhia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:12.480
is officially delayed until further notice. 
Victor now finally decides to leave the airport.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:17.440
As he moves towards the exit, everyone rushes&nbsp;
to see him off. They provide him with gifts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:22.640
and wish him the best for his journey. As Dixon&nbsp;
witnesses this, he orders the guards to stop him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:27.600
exiting the airport. At this point, only the&nbsp;
guards stand in between Victor and New York.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:32.560
Dixon then tells the guards to arrest him.&nbsp;
Officer Therman then tells Victor to turn around.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:36.720
As everyone anticipates that Victor will get&nbsp;
arrested, the officer covers him with a jacket&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:40.960
instead, saying that he’ll need an extra&nbsp;
layer since it’s snowing outside.
&nbsp;

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:46.640
Victor finally steps out of the door, after&nbsp;
an excruciatingly long wait of 9 months. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:52.880
then takes a taxi and leaves to meet Benny. Just&nbsp;
as he leaves, Dixon arrives outside. When asked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:57.840
if he wants to stop Victor, he simply replies&nbsp;
that he is tired of all this, and is in fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.840 --> 00:13:07.760
impressed by his sheer determination.
Victor arrives at a jazz club and finally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:12.880
meets Benny Goldson. He asks him for the&nbsp;
autograph but Benny suggests he wait a bit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:17.360
An emotional Victor then hears the group&nbsp;
perform, something which his father&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:22.240
would have loved. After the performance, Victor&nbsp;
gets the autograph and completes the collection&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:27.760
which his father started 40 years ago. He can&nbsp;
now finally return back to his home country. 
&nbsp;

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:33.360
In this movie, Victor spends a total of 9 months&nbsp;
at the airport. But Mehran Karimi Nasseri,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:38.080
the man whose life inspired this movie,&nbsp;
spent an astonishing 18 years at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:42.640
Charles de Gaulle Airport in Paris.
